        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "38622165-4b10-5f52-9cda-bf698d80731d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Užupis, Freetown Christiania, Belmontas, Rasos, Vilnia River, Paris, Copenhagen\n- Concepts: bohemic atmosphere, laissez-faire atmosphere, artist popularity, public closure and reopening\n\nFacts:\n- Užupis has been popular with artists for some time.\n- Užupis has been compared to Montmartre in Paris because of its bohemic and laissez-faire atmosphere.\n- Užupis has also been compared to Freetown Christiania in Copenhagen because of its bohemic and laissez-faire atmosphere.\n- In April 2011, residents of Freetown Christiania temporarily closed it to the public while discussions with the Danish government about its future continued.\n- After the April 2011 closure, Freetown Christiania re-opened to the public.\n- Belmontas is located in the area of Rasos on the right bank of the Vilnia River, east of Užupis.",
